# Introduction to CodeChef

CodeChef is an online competitive programming platform where programmers can practice coding, participate in contests, and improve their problem-solving skills. It provides problems of different difficulty levels and supports various programming languages such as C, C++, Java, and Python.

CodeChef helps students develop logical thinking, algorithm design, debugging skills, and coding efficiency. It is widely used by beginners as well as professional programmers to prepare for coding interviews and programming competitions.

---

# Program 1: Add Two Numbers

## Theory

This is one of the simplest programming problems on CodeChef. The objective is to read two integers and print their sum. The program demonstrates the use of input/output statements, variables, and arithmetic operators.

## Program

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main()
{
    int a, b;

    scanf("%d %d", &a, &b);

    printf("%d\n", a + b);

    return 0;
}
```

### Sample Input

```text
10 20
```

### Sample Output

```text
30
```

## Conclusion

The program successfully accepts two numbers from the user and displays their sum. It demonstrates the basic use of arithmetic operations and input/output functions in C.

