# Program 2: Find Remainder

## Theory

This program finds the remainder when one number is divided by another number. The modulus (%) operator is used to obtain the remainder after division.

## Program

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main()
{
    int a, b;

    scanf("%d %d", &a, &b);

    printf("%d\n", a % b);

    return 0;
}
```

### Sample Input

```text
17 5
```

### Sample Output

```text
2
```

## Conclusion

The program successfully calculates and displays the remainder obtained after dividing one number by another. It demonstrates the use of the modulus operator in C programming.

